+Aircade Development Roadmap
+
+Executive Summary
+
+Aircade is a retro-style 2D pixel-art survival adventure designed for offline play. In the game, the player
+survives a plane crash and must scavenge wreckage, manage health/hunger/thirst/stamina, craft tools,
+and overcome environmental hazards to escape. The game features a clear narrative (e.g. find water,
+build a shelter, repair a radio, activate a rescue beacon) rather than endless survival, ensuring each
+objective advances the story. As an offline-first title, all single-player content requires no internet
+(ideal for flights, trains, remote areas)πÇÉ20ΓÇáL124-L133πÇæ. Crucially, Aircade supports local Bluetooth
+P2P multiplayer: nearby devices connect directly (Host-Client model) without Wi-Fi, letting friends
+cooperatively or competitively survive together. This dual focus ΓÇô a polished offline solo experience plus
+seamless Bluetooth-based local multiplayer ΓÇô makes Aircade uniquely suited for travel and offline
+scenarios while keeping development fully free/open-source.
+
